cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this list in your work, please cite it as below. Developed by Zhenxian LI with assistance from Claude Code."
type: dataset
title: "LISQM: List of Implementations of Sound Quality Metrics"
abstract: >-
  LISQM (List of Implementations of Sound Quality Metrics) is a curated, monthly-refreshed list of
  open-source implementations of psychoacoustic metrics, also called sound quality metrics, in any
  programming language: loudness, sharpness, roughness, fluctuation strength, tonality, impulsiveness and
  psychoacoustic annoyance, with related quantities such as equal-loudness contours, effective perceived
  noise level (EPNL) and aural detectability. Each implementation is listed under the standard edition or
  model paper it follows (for example ISO 532-1, ECMA-418-2 or DIN 45692), together with its licence,
  packages, release activity and the validation evidence the project itself states. The list consists of
  data and a static website; it contains no metric code and does not run the listed software.
authors:
